                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915602,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 68.14,
                  "from": 63.74,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2915609,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "I'm going to report on a case study of a program which has been set up to help rural populations in Mozambique, a largely agricultural country in Southeast Africa. The program worked with three communities in Chikualakwala District near the Limpopo River. This is a dry and arid region with unpredictable rainfall. Because of this, people in the area were unable to support themselves through agriculture, and instead, they used the forest as a means of providing themselves with an income, mainly by selling charcoal. However, this was not a sustainable way of living in the long term as they were rapidly using up this resource.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2915610,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "I'm going to report on a case study of a program which has been set up to help rural populations in Mozambique, a largely agricultural country in Southeast Africa.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 84.325005,
                  "from": 71.525,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915640,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The program worked with three communities in Chikualakwala District near the Limpopo River.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 93.28,
                  "from": 85.76,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915654,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "This is a dry and arid region with unpredictable rainfall.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 99.36,
                  "from": 94.159996,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915665,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Because of this, people in the area were unable to support themselves through agriculture, and instead, they used the forest as a means of providing themselves with an income, mainly by selling charcoal.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 117.35,
                  "from": 100.835,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915698,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "However, this was not a sustainable way of living in the long term as they were rapidly using up this resource.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 128.31,
                  "from": 118.46999,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2915720,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "To support agriculture in this dry region, the program focused primarily on making use of existing water resources from the Limpopo River by setting up systems of irrigation, which would provide a dependable water supply for crops and animals. The program worked closely with the district government in order to find the best way of implementing this. The region already had one farmers association, and it was decided to set up two more of these. These associations planned and carried out activities including water management, livestock breeding, and agriculture. And it was notable that in general, women formed the majority of the workforce.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2915721,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "To support agriculture in this dry region, the program focused primarily on making use of existing water resources from the Limpopo River by setting up systems of irrigation, which would provide a dependable water supply for crops and animals.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 151.61,
                  "from": 130.305,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915761,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The program worked closely with the district government in order to find the best way of implementing this.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 161.355,
                  "from": 152.81,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915780,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The region already had one farmers association, and it was decided to set up two more of these.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 170.875,
                  "from": 162.635,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915799,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "These associations planned and carried out activities including water management, livestock breeding, and agriculture.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 182.69002,
                  "from": 172.45001,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915814,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "And it was notable that in general, women formed the majority of the workforce.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 190.03502,
                  "from": 183.25,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2915829,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "It was decided that in order to keep the crops safe from animals, both wild and domestic, special areas should be fenced off where the crops could be grown. The community was responsible for creating these fences, but the program provided the necessary wire for making them. Once the area had been fenced off, it could be cultivated. The land was dug so that vegetables and cereals appropriate to the climate could be grown, and the program provided the necessary seeds for this. The program also provided pumps so that water could be brought from the river in pipes to the fields.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2915830,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "It was decided that in order to keep the crops safe from animals, both wild and domestic, special areas should be fenced off where the crops could be grown.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 205.21,
                  "from": 192.115,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2915860,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The community was responsible for creating these fences, but the program provided the necessary wire for making them.",
